# KeySync Lite – Property & Real Estate Domain Rules

## Domain Context

KeySync Lite is a lead intelligence system specifically designed for **Dubai real estate brokerages**. All AI analysis, responses, and knowledge retrieval should be grounded in Dubai's property market context.

---

## Dubai Real Estate Specifics

### Key Areas & Neighborhoods

- **Luxury Areas**: Palm Jumeirah, Downtown Dubai, Dubai Marina, Emirates Hills, Jumeirah
- **Off-Plan Hotspots**: Dubai Creek Harbour, Sobha Hartland, Business Bay, Dubai Hills Estate
- **Rental-Friendly**: JVC (Jumeirah Village Circle), Sports City, Al Barsha, JLT (Jumeirah Lakes Towers)
- **Emerging**: Dubai South, Dubai Land, Arjan

### Property Types & Terminology

- **Villa**: Standalone house (typically 3BR+, often with pool/garden)
- **Apartment/Flat**: Multi-unit residential building
- **Studio**: Single room with kitchenette and bathroom
- **1BR/2BR/3BR**: Bedroom count
- **Off-Plan**: Pre-construction properties (payment plans, handover dates matter)
- **Ready**: Completed properties (immediate possession)
- **Furnished/Unfurnished**: Rental property condition

### Budget Ranges (AED)

- **Budget Rental**: 30k–60k AED/year (studios, 1BR in JVC/Sports City)
- **Mid-Range Rental**: 60k–120k AED/year (2BR in JVC, 1BR in Marina)
- **Premium Rental**: 120k+ AED/year (2BR+ in Marina, Downtown)
- **Budget Purchase**: 500k–1.5M AED (studios, 1BR in emerging areas)
- **Mid-Range Purchase**: 1.5M–4M AED (2BR apartments, small villas)
- **Luxury Purchase**: 4M+ AED (villas, penthouses, prime locations)

### Common Client Types

- **Investor**: Focus on ROI, rental yield, payment plans, capital appreciation
- **End-User**: Focus on location, schools, commute, lifestyle, move-in readiness
- **Expat**: Often needs furnished, proximity to work/schools, visa considerations
- **Local/Emirati**: May prefer villas, larger spaces, family-friendly areas

